rain-core: xray/0050-muxcool-write-deadlines
Source: ReClash fix on top of xray/0037 (GPL-3.0).

A peer that stopped reading could pin the carrier write turn forever: every
session queued behind writeMu, and Close waited on an End frame behind the
same turn. Serialize frames with a token that a caller can wait on with its
own deadline, and bound one whole frame write with a 30 s carrier timeout
(options.write-timeout is not exposed; the pool default applies). A timeout
while waiting for the turn writes nothing and leaves the carrier usable; a
timeout inside the physical write closes the carrier because the frame may be
partial. packetSession.WriteTo now carries its deadline through the turn wait
and the physical write, and reports os.ErrDeadlineExceeded without killing the
carrier when nothing was written.

Tests: TestCarrierWriteTimeoutClosesStalledCarrier,
TestPacketWriteDeadlineBoundsCarrierTurnWait,
TestPacketWriteDeadlineDuringPhysicalWriteClosesCarrier,
TestCarrierPartialWriteClosesCarrier.

